        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The <b>current ratio</b> measures a company's ability to pay short-term obligations with its current assets. It is calculated as: $ \text{Current Ratio} = \frac{\text{Current Assets}}{\text{Current Liabilities}} $.</p>",
